Run the local agent-facing proxy on `127.0.0.1:<port>`.

Agent CLIs point at it via `OPENAI_BASE_URL`. The proxy discovers providers, picks the cheapest one for each model, and signs each request via two-tier vouchers.

Usage: soma inference proxy [OPTIONS] --indexer-url <INDEXER_URL>

Options:
      --address <ADDRESS>
          Address whose key signs both on-chain ops and HTTP vouchers. Defaults to the wallet's active address

      --client <CLIENT>
          Path to the soma client config (defaults to ~/.soma/client.yaml)

      --soma-home <SOMA_HOME>
          Soma home (for the off-chain provider registry + per-channel client state). Defaults to ~/.soma

      --listen <LISTEN>
          HTTP listen address
          
          [default: 127.0.0.1:11434]

      --default-deposit-micros <DEFAULT_DEPOSIT_MICROS>
          Default deposit (micros) when lazily opening a new channel
          
          [default: 5000000]

      --provider-cache-ttl-secs <PROVIDER_CACHE_TTL_SECS>
          Provider-list cache TTL (seconds)
          
          [default: 30]

      --routing <ROUTING>
          Provider-routing mode: `price` (default) or `weighted`. `weighted` requires reputation from the indexer
          
          [default: price]

      --indexer-url <INDEXER_URL>
          GraphQL HTTP endpoint of the indexer. Required: provider discovery and (in `weighted` mode) reputation are sourced from here

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

EXAMPLE:
    soma inference proxy --listen 127.0.0.1:11434
